course: dictionary
lesson: 11805
title: Beverage: a word for drink
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A beverage is a formal word for a drink. You will see it on menus, on signs and in exam texts, and it is more common in the USA. «Please choose a hot beverage from the menu.» Here the word beverage simply means drink, and hot tells you it is warm.
explain: Beverage can mean any kind of drink, such as water, juice, tea or milk. «The café sold cold beverages on a hot day.» The clues are cold and hot day, so beverages must mean drinks that are cold and fresh. Ask yourself: what word would fit here? Then try drink in the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
explain: Some signs use alcoholic beverage. «No alcoholic beverages are sold to children.» The word alcoholic tells you this means drinks like beer and wine, which are not for young people. Words like food and beverages often appear together, meaning things to eat and things to drink.
fact: «Beverage» means a drink of any kind.
fact: Water, milk, juice and tea are all beverages.
fact: «Alcoholic beverage» means a drink like beer or wine, as used on some signs and menus.
fact: «Food and beverages» means things to eat and things to drink.
fact: In maths problems, beverages can be priced and counted, just like apples or pencils.
exercise: «The café sold cold beverages on a hot day.» What does beverages mean here? | Plates | Chairs | Books | *Drinks
exercise: Which of these is a beverage? | A sandwich | A chair | *Milk | A cake
exercise: Sam buys 3 beverages that cost 2 dollars each. How many dollars does he pay in total? | 1 | *6 | 5 | 23
test: On a menu, what is an alcoholic beverage? | A pencil | A cake | A bus ticket | *A drink like beer or wine
test: Which phrase names things to eat and things to drink? | Cold pencils | *Food and beverages | Loud music | Blue hats
exam: Which word is a formal word for drink? | Chair | Shoe | *Beverage | Bread
